    "content": "At the 2026 Boston Marathon, Kenyan runner John Korir set a new men's course record of 2:01:52. This surpassed the 15-year-old record of 2:03:02 set by Geoffrey Mutai in 2011. Sharon Lokedi of Kenya won the 2026 women's division in 2:18:51, defending her 2025 title, while Marcel Hug holds the men's wheelchair record (1:16:06) set in 2024.Boston Marathon Records (Updated April 2026):Men's Open: John Korir (KEN), 2:01:52 (2026)Women's Open: Hellen Obiri (KEN), 2:19:59 (2024)*Men's Wheelchair: Marcel Hug (SUI), 1:16:06 (2024)Women's Wheelchair: Manuela Schär (SUI), 1:28:17 (2017)Note: Sharon Lokedi ran 2:18:51 at the 2026 race according to early reports, though official, finalized records usually take time to be confirmed. John Korir's 2026 victory was immediately recognized as a new course record, shaving over a minute off the previous mark.",
